abstract: >-
  The SAR Morocco Flood Dataset provides 1,497 co-registered Sentinel-1 SAR
  patches (256 x 256 pixels, dual-polarization VV+VH) and corresponding binary
  water masks distributed across five hydrological zones in northern-central
  Morocco. The dataset covers recent hydrological events documented between
  September 2024 and April 2026, including the Ksar El Kebir flood
  (January-February 2026), the Gharb plain flood (February 2026), reservoir
  states at contrasting seasons (Al Wahda, summer 2024 and winter 2025), the
  SMBA post-drought filling (March 2026), and the Bin El Ouidane reservoir at
  high winter filling (winter 2026). Water masks were generated
  semi-automatically using the Hierarchical Split-Based Approach (HSBA)
  combined with Otsu thresholding and morphological post-processing, followed
  by two-pass visual quality control. All data are provided as georeferenced
  GeoTIFF files with per-patch CSV metadata and zone-level Markdown
  documentation. The dataset supports training and evaluation of deep learning
  models for SAR-based flood mapping in Mediterranean and North African
  contexts.

